        ("Assertion-Reason: Divisional Structure and Growth", "Given below are two statements labeled as Assertion (A) and Reason (R):\nAssertion (A): A divisional structure facilitates rapid enterprise expansion and addition of new product lines.\nReason (R): A new product line can be added as an independent division without interrupting the operations of existing divisions.\nSelect the correct option:", "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).", "Both (A) and (R) are true, but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).", "(A) is true, but (R) is false.", "(A) is false, but (R) is true.", "Autonomous divisions allow new lines to be launched seamlessly without disrupting existing business units."),
        ("Statement I & II: Functional Head vs Divisional Head", "Given below are two statements labeled as Statement I and Statement II:\nStatement I: A functional head gains comprehensive multi-disciplinary skills in manufacturing, marketing, and finance simultaneously.\nStatement II: A divisional head has broader managerial development because they oversee all functional areas within their product division.\nChoose the correct option:", "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "Functional heads specialize in one function only, whereas divisional heads oversee all functions within their unit."),
        ("Statement I & II: Span of Management", "Given below are two statements labeled as Statement I and Statement II:\nStatement I: Span of management refers to the number of subordinates that can be effectively managed by a superior.\nStatement II: Span of management determines the levels of management in an organizational hierarchy.\nChoose the correct option:", "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "Both statements correctly reflect NCERT doctrine on span of management and hierarchical depth."),
        ("Span of Management: Wide vs Narrow Span", "When a manager can effectively supervise a large number of subordinates, the resulting organizational structure is characterized by:", "A wide span of management resulting in a flat organizational structure", "A narrow span of management resulting in a tall organizational structure", "An infinite span of management eliminating all managerial positions", "A divisional structure with zero delegation", "A wide span means more subordinates per manager, resulting in fewer hierarchical tiers (flat structure)."),
