        ("Delegation vs Decentralisation: Scope", "Match List-I (Parameter) with List-II (Delegation vs Decentralisation Difference):\nList-I:\n(A) Scope\n(B) Nature\n(C) Freedom of Action\n(D) Purpose\n\nList-II:\n(I) An optional corporate policy decision\n(II) Limited scope confined to superior and immediate subordinate\n(III) Subordinates enjoy substantial operational autonomy\n(IV) To lessen the burden of the manager\nChoose the correct option:", "(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)", "(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)", "(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)", "(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)", "Scope: limited in delegation (II); Nature: decentralisation is optional policy (I); Freedom: greater in decentralisation (III); Purpose of delegation: lessen manager's burden (IV)."),
        ("Decentralisation: Develops Initiative among Subordinates", "When lower-level managers are given the freedom to formulate their own operational solutions, they learn to rely on their own judgment. This illustrates:", "Develops Initiative among Subordinates", "Quick Decision Making Alone", "Relief to Top Management Alone", "Better Control Alone", "Decentralisation fosters self-reliance, initiative, and creative problem-solving among lower-level managers."),
